// The wingflight package: wings and flight for any rig with wing chains. A program reaches it with
// 'import wingflight'.
//
// - Wings (wings.cone): wings found in a rig by kind; the flap cycle (a downstroke and an upstroke with the joints
//   lagging), the fold and unfold, the glide dihedral, the twist; feather fans that spread and close; all the
//   numbers in WingParams.
// - Surfaces (surfaces.cone): feather fans added to a RigSpec as data and their blades made into a mesh;
//   membranes stretched between lines of anchors on the bones, made into a mesh; each with skinning weights.
// - Aerodynamics (aero.cone): lift and drag over every angle of attack (the finite-wing slope below the stall,
//   Viterna's extrapolation above) and the force on a flapping section.
// - Flight (flight.cone): the Flier, a point mass driven by the force of its wings, with an autopilot
//   for takeoff, climb, cruise, glide, banking turns, flare and landing, and the poses to draw it.
// - Samples (samples.cone): a plain feathered wing and a plain membrane wing, for tests and demos.
//
// It sits on creaturerig (the Rig and its chains), bonepose, poseik (pose blending) and mesh. The flight and the wing
// pose do not depend on the legs: leggedgait's pose may be laid under the flight (see `compose`).
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: metres, right handed, y up, a creature faces -z at yaw 0, a positive yaw turns it
// left, its right is +x. A bank is positive for the right wing down.
//
//   wingflight.cone   this overview
//   aero.cone         Aero, coefficients, sectionForce
//   wings.cone        WingParams, Wings, WingMotion, poseWings
//   surfaces.cone     addFeatherFan, featherMesh, MembraneStrip, membraneMesh
//   flight.cone       Flier, Goal, compose
//   samples.cone      plainFeathers, plainMembrane

mod wingflight;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
import poseik use *;
import creaturerig use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
